\ results/drafts/hashk-727.4 - the gene hashk's prototype (Iteration 727; results/drafts/demoscene-ioccc-727.md): the
\ chain hash multiplicative, ((v * K) & 0xFFFF) >> (16 - log2 #threads), K searched per image on the held-out programs
\ (results/drafts/hashseed-727.py). Loaded last among a design's overlays by results/drafts/hashk-727.py: HASH8's body
\ becomes HASH's (tools/layout.py's X8 swap); the converter threads the image with the same K (HASHK=K in its
\ environment, the scratch tree's tools/layout.py). K and the shift are this prototype's literals, set by the harness:
\ 2643 and 9 for 128 chains - the smallest's.
: HASH8 ( c-addr u #threads --- n )
  >R OVER C@ 1 LSHIFT OVER 1 > IF ROT 1+ C@ 2 LSHIFT XOR ELSE ROT DROP
   THEN XOR
  R> DROP 2643 * 65535 AND 9 RSHIFT ;
